    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d639">

                <pb facs="0617" n="445" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp01v01/pg445"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4729</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        French Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jusserand</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1853</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-19">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1917</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 12th instant in which you communicate to me the
                    views of the President of the Council, Minister for Foreign Affairs of the
                    French Republic, regarding the importance to the interests of the nations in
                    arms against Germany of a rupture of the diplomatic relations between Siam and
                    Germany.</p>
                <p>The American Government having in February last suggested to the Government of
                    Siam that it would make for the peace of the world if the neutral powers could
                    find it possible to take action similar to that of the United States by breaking
                    off diplomatic relations with Germany, and having been told in reply that while
                    the Siamese Government sympathized with the motives of the United States they
                    preferred to maintain neutrality, the present moment does not appear to me to be
                    opportune for a renewal of the suggestion.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
